<section style="padding:96px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Oil tank removal in St. John's isn't something you can put off. Under NLR 60/03, the Heating Oil Storage Tank System Regulations, a disconnected tank has to be emptied, dismantled and disposed of within 30 days, and within 10 days if it leaked or took on water. Harbour Tank Co does the whole job: we pump out the leftover oil, clean out the sludge, take the tank apart, cap the lines and take everything away.</p><p>Most people call us for one of three reasons. The tag expired and the delivery driver wouldn't fill, they've switched to electric heat and the old tank is still sitting there, or a leak forced the issue. Whatever brought you here, you'll get a free written estimate, a flat $500 price on outdoor tanks, and a crew that knows the rules. Call (709) 800-3117, or keep reading for what's involved.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Handle</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What's Included in Every Visit</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Flat $500 outdoor removal</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A standard outdoor domestic tank is removed and disposed of for $500 CAD. That's the number on the estimate and the number on the invoice.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Indoor and basement tanks</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Basement tanks have to be cut down and carried out in pieces. We check the access and quote each one in writing before any work starts.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Oil and sludge dealt with properly</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Residual oil is pumped out and the sludge at the bottom is scraped out and taken away. Nothing goes down a drain or into the ground.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Lines capped or pulled</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Fill and vent pipes are capped or removed so nobody can ever fill a tank that isn't there.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Site put back the way it was</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Stand, pad, brackets and debris leave with us. We rake the ground or sweep the basement floor before we go.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">24/7 emergency line</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Leaking tank, or a refused delivery in a January cold snap? Call (709) 800-3117 any hour.</p>
      </div>
</div>
